/-!
# The M₂₂ and M₂₃ rows of the original local Cartan sieve

For the same containing component selected by the escape reduction, the
five-square-free Mathieu orders force the seed to equal the whole residual.
The original source alternatives, restricted full Sylow and native Mathieu
local geometry then identify its literal two-core quotient as PSL₂(4).
The original right Hall condition gives a subgroup of order three.

In M₂₂ the solvable subgroup generated by the original Sylow and both Hall
factors has inner image of order 384. Its odd action is therefore already
the right cubic action, which normalizes the residual. This excludes M₂₂.
The reduction retains M₂₃ with its proved residual and Hall conclusions,
alongside every earlier exclusion and the full binary-triality endpoint.
The escaping inverted cubic and exhaustive non-rank-two sieve remain open.

The private finite-order lemmas are reused through `import all` within this
source development, preserving their existing module boundary.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 5.1.12--13, printed pp.635--637,
refs/quasithin.pdf; native Mathieu local geometry as used in A.3.12--14.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory BenderSuzuki.MatrixGroups
